{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote\/isChord"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this note is an additional chord tone with the preceding note."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isChord"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The duration of a chord note does not move the musical position within a measure. That is done by the duration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the first preceding note without a chord element. Thus the duration of a chord note cannot be longer than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the preceding note. In most cases the duration will be the same as the preceding note. However, it can be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"shorter in situations such as multiple stops for string instruments."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"<chord>"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfullnote\/ischord"]}],"sections":[],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","title":"isChord","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isChord"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","text":"Bool"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL11MXLFullNoteV7isChordSbvp","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFullNote/isChord":{"abstract":[{"text":"A Boolean value indicating whether this note is an additional chord tone with the preceding note.","type":"text"}],"title":"isChord","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote\/isChord","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfullnote\/ischord","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"isChord"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Bool","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLFullNote":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlfullnote","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLFullNote","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The full-note group is a sequence of the common note elements between cue\/grace notes and regular (full)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"notes: pitch, chord, and rest information, but not duration (cue and grace notes do not have duration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"encoded). Unpitched elements are used for unpitched percussion, speaking voice, and other musical elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lacking determinate pitch."}],"title":"MXLFullNote","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLFullNote","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLFullNote","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"}}}